{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "10: Context-insights sync",
  "description": "End-to-end: the secondary, best-effort upload that reports per-customization-file counts (never contents) for the same window as the aggregate batch, and its strict server-side validation. Every step embeds the numbered sequence diagram and points at the exact code for that step.",
  "nextTour": "11: Context hotspots",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Step 1 — Best-effort secondary send",
      "file": "src/core/agent-observability-core/src/sync/syncEngine.ts",
      "line": 388,
      "description": "![10: Context-insights sync](.tours/diagrams/d-70.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 1 of 7 in the sequence diagram — `SyncEngine → syncClient: sendContextInsights(rows)`**\n\nAfter a successful aggregate sync (flow 7), the engine sends a SEPARATE context-insights batch for the same window via `client.sendContextInsights(batch)`. It is fully isolated — any failure here never affects the aggregate result."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 2 — POST context-insights",
      "file": "src/core/agent-observability-core/src/sync/syncClient.ts",
      "line": 132,
      "description": "![10: Context-insights sync](.tours/diagrams/d-71.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 2 of 7 in the sequence diagram — `syncClient → IngestionEndpoints: POST /api/ingest/context-insights`**\n\n`SyncClient.sendContextInsights` mirrors `sendBatch` byte-for-byte in transport, auth, and scrubbing — only the path differs: `POST {dashboardUrl}/api/ingest/context-insights`."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 3 — Validate the contract",
      "file": "src/dashboard/AgentObservability.Dashboard/Services/Ingestion/ContextInsightsBatchValidator.cs",
      "line": 47,
      "description": "![10: Context-insights sync](.tours/diagrams/d-72.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 3 of 7 in the sequence diagram — `IngestionEndpoints → ContextInsightsValidator: Validate(batch)`**\n\nServer-side, `Validate` enforces the context-insights contract — `additionalProperties:false` at every level, so only repo-relative customization-file paths and counts are accepted, never file contents."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 4 — Reject on error",
      "file": "src/dashboard/AgentObservability.Dashboard/Services/Ingestion/IngestionEndpoints.cs",
      "line": 194,
      "description": "![10: Context-insights sync](.tours/diagrams/d-73.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 4 of 7 in the sequence diagram — `ContextInsightsValidator → IngestionEndpoints: errors or ok`**\n\nValidation failures return a 400 ValidationProblem; the batch is rejected whole."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 5 — Upsert rows, scoped to org",
      "file": "src/dashboard/AgentObservability.Dashboard/Services/Ingestion/IngestionEndpoints.cs",
      "line": 201,
      "description": "![10: Context-insights sync](.tours/diagrams/d-74.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 5 of 7 in the sequence diagram — `IngestionEndpoints → TableContextInsightStore: UpsertRowsAsync(orgId)`**\n\nA valid batch is stored with `store.UpsertRowsAsync(auth.OrgId!, batch)`, scoped to the authenticated org from the key record — never the payload."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 6 — Idempotent row write",
      "file": "src/dashboard/AgentObservability.Dashboard/Services/Ingestion/TableContextInsightStore.cs",
      "line": 29,
      "description": "![10: Context-insights sync](.tours/diagrams/d-75.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 6 of 7 in the sequence diagram — `TableContextInsightStore → IngestionEndpoints: stored (idempotent rowKey)`**\n\n`TableContextInsightStore.UpsertRowsAsync` upserts each row under a deterministic row key, so re-sending the same window is idempotent."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 7 — 200 accepted",
      "file": "src/dashboard/AgentObservability.Dashboard/Services/Ingestion/IngestionEndpoints.cs",
      "line": 203,
      "description": "![10: Context-insights sync](.tours/diagrams/d-76.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 7 of 7 in the sequence diagram — `IngestionEndpoints → syncClient: 200 accepted`**\n\nThe handler returns `200 Ok` with the accepted row count and batch id, completing the secondary upload."
    }
  ]
}
